            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KKlovesJC"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just made this at Christmas to go with the tenderloin I served. The horseradish sauce i bought was quite hot so I simply whipped 1/4c more heavy cream and added a dash more sugar and also added some orange rind. Delicious! Rave reviews from everyone! \nLove and blessings!",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-26T16:04:35.807Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lindsay Beveridge"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the absolute best with prime rib! I make this often as a treat to go along with all sorts of beef. As far as another review that called it bitter - you need to make sure you drain the prepared horseradish out of the jar. Squeeze all of the liquid out of it before you add it to the recipe. Make sure to use full fat mayo and the Dijon mustard is a must. This sauce has just the right amount of all the ingredients!!!",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-14T19:22:30.470Z"
          },
